1	# Project Motivation
2	
3	This is part of a greater idea to automate mobile pentesting with multiple agents that communicate over a protocol like A2A. This is a rough draft version where not all the tooling may work. It is possible to use stdio versions of this mcp server to make setup easier, but the intent of this is to have completely isolated devices that can cross-communicate on a network. **Use at your own risk.**
4	
5	# Known Issues (both platforms)
6	
7	- Different AI models will have varied success on invoking the correct tool
8	- The 0.15.2 5ire release might break AI invocation, it's better to just [manually run the project with node](https://github.com/nanbingxyz/5ire/blob/main/DEVELOPMENT.md)
9	- Session management is not implemented, so if you kill a process there will be a dangling session and there is no way to list interactive sessions
10	- Tool prompts need to be reworked to help the agents pick the tool more accurately
11	- No graceful shutdown on the server
12	- **Security in general is not implemented.** Your messages can be sniffed and they do not require authorization. **Use at your own risk.**
13	
14	# Workstation Requirements
15	
16	- An MCP-compatible client with streamable HTTP support. Going forward, development is targeting [Gemini CLI](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli) and [Claude Code](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/claude-code/overview), since both are building native multi-agent orchestration that aligns with this project's direction.
17	
18	  - **Gemini CLI** — add the on-device server (replace `<DEVICE_IP>`):
19	
20	    ```bash
21	    gemini mcp add --transport http frida-c2-mcp http://<DEVICE_IP>:6767/mcp
22	    ```
23	
24	  - [5ire](https://github.com/nanbingxyz/5ire) is a great GUI option and was used extensively during development. If using 5ire: the 0.15.2 release has a Gemini invocation issue on Windows — run as a node project via [this guide](https://github.com/nanbingxyz/5ire/blob/main/DEVELOPMENT.md) with node `22.19.0` and `npm run dev -- --no-sandbox --disable-gpu`.
25	
26	  - Point your client at the device's MCP endpoint. Example config (5ire format):
27	
28	  ```
29	  {
30	  "name": "fridaMCP",
31	  "key": "frida",
32	  "url": "http://<phone_ip>:6767/mcp",
33	  "approvalPolicy": "always"
34	  }
35	  ```
36	
37	---
38	
39	# Android Setup (`cli.py`)
40	
41	## Tested on
42	
43	- Pixel 9 running Android 16 API 36
44	- Magisk 30.4
45	- Frida 17.2.14
46	- 5ire with Gemini 2.5 Flash
47	
48	## Device Requirements
49	
50	- A rooted Android device
51	
52	  - Take a look at the process with [Magisk](https://github.com/topjohnwu/Magisk)
53	
54	  - You can use an emulator, but a physical device is cooler :3 also with the emulator the networking isn't immediately obvious to setup, you'll have to use adb port forwarding or a non-standard network bridge in whatever emulator you're using
55	
56	  - Unless you're dealing with sensitive data on the device just set Magisk to auto approve any superuser request
57	
58	- A Frida server
59	
60	  - Just use the latest [Frida Magisk module](https://github.com/ViRb3/magisk-frida/releases). Make sure to match the client version of the Frida you choose to use / compile
61	
62	- Install termux
63	
64	  - Use the [GitHub version of termux](https://github.com/termux/termux-app)
65	
66	- Inside of termux install the root repo 
67	
68	  - `pkg install root-repo`
69	
70	- Inside of termux install all the packages (I might be missing stuff here)
71	
72	  - The following should install necessary build tools: `pkg install git python clang gcc rust nodejs ninja pkg-config libresolv-wrapper wget` 
73	
74	  - Do NOT install frida with pip -- it will fail cuz of the C bindings.
75	
76	- Manually build the Frida client
77	
78	  - Find the latest frida-core-devkit for the appropriate architecture and use `wget` to grab the .xz file
79	
80	  - `mkdir -p frida-core && tar -xf <yourdevkit.tar.xz> -C frida-core`
81	
82	  - Grab the frida-python project `git clone https://github.com/frida/frida-python.git`
83	
84	- Run the following (there might be missing steps here)
85	
86	```
87	# This config should work but if it gives you trouble try hardcoding all the paths instead of using $HOME references
88	
89	export HOME=/data/data/com.termux/files/home
90	export PREFIX=/data/data/com.termux/files/usr
91	export FRIDA_CORE_DEVKIT="$HOME/frida-core"
92	export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/frida-core"
93	
94	# CHANGE THIS BASED ON WHAT ARCHITECTURE YOU'RE ON
95	
96	cd $HOME/frida-python/deps/toolchain-linux-arm64/bin/
97	
98	# Some of the toolchain native binaries are broken so we'll swap them out here
